### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)

```turtle
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

# Entities
ex:Vehicle_1 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:hasType "Sedan" ;
    ex:position "moving" ;
    ex:color "black" .

ex:Vehicle_2 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:hasType "Convertible" ;
    ex:position "stationary" ;
    ex:color "white" .

ex:Vehicle_3 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:hasType "Mini" ;
    ex:position "moving" ;
    ex:color "silver" .

ex:Pedestrian_1 a ex:Pedestrian ;
    ex:position "not_present" .

ex:Road a ex:Infrastructure ;
    ex:hasCondition "wet" ;
    ex:hasWeather "rainy" .

ex:Overpass a ex:Infrastructure ;
    ex:hasType "bridge" ;
    ex:position "above" .

# Relationships
ex:Vehicle_1 ex:approaches ex:Vehicle_2 .
ex:Vehicle_2 ex:following ex:Vehicle_1 .
ex:Vehicle_1 ex:crosses ex:road .
ex:Vehicle_2 ex:near ex:Road .
ex:Vehicle_3 ex:near ex:Vehicle_1 .
ex:Vehicle_1 ex:occludes ex:Vehicle_3 .
```

### Identified Risks for each risk class

**Risk 1:**
Description: Potential collision between Vehicle 1 (black sedan) and Vehicle 2 (white convertible) while navigating a wet road under an overpass.
Severity Score: 0.7

**Risk 2:**
Description: Reduced braking effectiveness due to wet road conditions, increasing the likelihood of loss of control.
Severity Score: 0.8

**Risk 3:**
Description: Visibility issues due to rain impairing the driver's ability to see road conditions and other vehicles clearly.
Severity Score: 0.6

**Risk 4:**
Description: Risk of skidding or hydroplaning from rapid maneuvers on the wet road surface.
Severity Score: 0.7